10th gen processors at the same time?

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:56.500
There still wouldn’t be much of a difference
in price and we would still recommend people

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:57.500
to just buy the base model.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:01.110
Being Apple, it would make more sense to upgrade
the higher-end 13” model first and keep

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:05.729
the base model the same, because honestly,
you’re already getting a ton of performance

00:02:05.729 --> 00:02:07.430
for the price.

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:11.810
So if this ends up happening, you’ll be
extremely disappointed if you waited for close

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:16.870
to a year for the 14” and you found out
that you have to pay at least $1800 to get

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:21.050
