00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:09.590
For Reason #3, this base model has the 4th-gen
butterfly keyboard.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:13.200
Now I know that makes you want to skip out
on this model altogether, but you may not

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.980
know that with this version of the butterfly
keys, Apple replaced a few of the key materials

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:23.500
with more reliable ones, and since the 2019
models, there has yet to be any reports of

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:24.540
failed keys.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:30.780
Yes, the new Magic keyboard feels a lot better,
but the main reason that Apple has switched

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:33.910
to the new Magic keyboard on the 16” MacBook
Pro is because people don’t trust the name

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:38.980
“Butterfly keyboard” anymore, so Apple
had to completely ditch that name for people

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:41.980
to feel more comfortable about purchasing
a new MacBook.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:48.170
For Reason #4, the performance boost going
from this models 8th gen CPU to the new 10th

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:49.370
gen isn’t that much.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:55.190
We’ve already had our hands on two Windows
laptops that pack Intel’s 10th gen processors,

00:03:55.190 --> 00:04:01.400
the Surface Laptop 3 with the lower-end i5
CPU and the XPS 13 2 in 1 with slightly better

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.690
i7 CPU.

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:07.430
Looking at multi-core processing performance
in Geekbench 5, the score only went up by

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:11.150
around 400-800 points depending on the chip.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:18.150
That’s 10-20% more CPU performance, which
honestly isn’t that big of a deal.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:26.360
Now for graphics, we get a much bigger difference,
from a score of 7358 up to 10434, which is

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:29.259
around a 40% boost in graphics performance.

00:04:29.259 --> 00:04:33.199
That’s definitely a good reason to wait
if you’re a graphics user, but for those

00:04:33.199 --> 00:04:37.169
of you who don’t do any kind of graphics
work, there’s no reason to wait.

00:04:37.169 --> 00:04:42.300
For Reason #5, technology is always moving
forward, and yet there are people who wait

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:47.879
for years and years because they keep hearing
rumors of better MacBooks being worked on.

00:04:47.879 --> 00:04:53.690
The truth is, you’re gonna have to buy one
some time, and Apple WILL release a better

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:56.520
model with better value eventually.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:01.599
My take on it is that instead of sitting around
and waiting for 6 months or maybe even close

00:05:01.599 --> 00:05:07.139
to a year, you can buy a MacBook Pro with
excellent performance right now and enjoy

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:10.490
it for all of those months that you would
have been waiting.

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:15.090
Those extra months of enjoyment are worth
it even if Apple releases a 14” MacBook

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:21.440
Pro next year, and if they only update the
higher-end $1800 model to 14 inches, you’ll

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:26.770
be extremely happy that you got this base
MacBook Pro for only $1100.

